## Quick Start

Install and run the guided setup:

```bash
brew install control-theory/dstl8/dstl8
dstl8 setup
```

`dstl8 setup` is the fastest path. It can create or detect your account,
install the MCP server into detected AI coding agents, auto-detect data
sources, and open the TUI or dashboard.

## High-Value Commands

- `dstl8 setup`
  Guided onboarding for account, MCP install, sources, and dashboard
- `dstl8 version`
  Confirm the installed CLI version
- `dstl8 tui`
  Open the terminal UI
- `dstl8 dashboard`
  Alias for `dstl8 tui`
- `dstl8 logs fetch -n 5`
  Fetch a few recent log lines
- `dstl8 sources`
  Show connected sources
- `dstl8 profiles`
  Show configured login profiles
- `dstl8 install status`
  Show where the MCP server is installed

## AI Agent Integration

Install into supported clients:

```bash
dstl8 install codex
dstl8 install claude-code
dstl8 install --include-experimental cursor
dstl8 install --all
dstl8 install status
```

Useful flags:

- `--project`
  Install project-scoped MCP config instead of user-scoped config
- `--dry-run`
  Preview config changes without writing them
- `--include-experimental`
  Include experimental clients such as Cursor

Restart the AI client after installation so it picks up the new MCP server.

